.TH reboot "" "Administration"
.SH NAME
reboot \- flush the file systems and restart the machine
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fB/etc/reboot\fR
.SH DESCRIPTION
.HS
reboot -- flush the file systems and restart the machine
Usage:	/etc/reboot
This command takes no options and may be run only by the superuser.
.HE
.B reboot
calls
.B sync()
twice and then calls the
.B reboot()
system call.
.B reboot()
marks every file system clean, flushes the buffer cache, and jumps to
the ROM restart entry; it does not return except on failure.
.PP
Only the superuser may reboot the machine: if
.B reboot()
fails (which happens when the caller is not the superuser), it
returns instead of restarting the machine, and
.B reboot
prints a diagnostic on the standard error and exits with status 1.
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.B sync
.SH DIAGNOSTICS
If the
.B reboot()
system call fails,
.B reboot
prints
.RS
.B "reboot: cannot reboot (not super-user?)"
.RE
on the standard error and exits with status 1.
